x` exists, and I've read its contents. I'm ready to move forward. My focus now is on precisely executing the line-based split with the given prime number chunk sizes, ensuring accurate file naming and graceful handling of any remainder lines.\\n\\n\\n\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thought\":true,\"text\":\"**Structuring the Splitting**\\n\\nI'm now zeroing in on the line splitting process. Using the file's content, the next steps are clear. I'm preparing a loop to iterate through the given chunk sizes. Inside the loop, I'll extract the corresponding number of lines, and write each chunk to its own uniquely named file, such as `crane.nix.part_1_2lines`, tracking the current line index to make it work. I've considered that the remaining lines may not completely match up, and will prepare for the edge case.\\n\\n\\n\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thought\":true,\"text\":\"**Executing the Split**\\n\\nI'm now formulating the execution plan. The intent is clear: split the file into chunks using the specified prime numbers. I've already confirmed the file exists and have its content. My next step is to create the output files, naming them based on the line count and chunk number. I'm focusing on the loop that will create these files.\\n\\n\\n\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thought\":true,\"text\":\"**Formulating the Loop**\\n\\nI'm now fully immersed in the core logic. My intent is to split the file, so I'm outlining the loop to iterate through the prime number chunk sizes. Inside, I'll extract lines, create new files with the specified naming convention, and carefully manage the remaining l