 handles embedding Git revisions for release builds.\\n*   **Workspace-wide Checks:** The module defines `checks` for the entire Rust workspace, including `clippy`, `test`, and `doc` generation.\\n*   **Individual Crate Checks:** An ambitious `all-crates-buildable-individually` check attempts to verify each crate with various feature combinations, though it's noted as currently broken. A simpler `check-all-workspace-members-individually` shell script is also provided.\\n*   **Dependency Vendoring:** It uses `crane.lib.vendorCargoDeps` to vendor dependencies, including a specific `postPatch` to address an issue with the `zhiburt/tabled` crate.\\n*   **Debugging and TODOs:** The file contains commented-out debugging aids and several `TODO` and `FIXME` comments indicating areas for future improvement or known issues (e.g., `rust-coverage` is currently disabled due to an Internal Compiler Error).\\n\\n**Overall Assessment:**\\n\\nThis `crane.nix` file is a powerful and well-structured solution for managing complex Rust projects within Nix. It prioritizes build efficiency, configurability, and comprehensive testing. The main areas for immediate attention are resolving the issues with the `all-crates-buildable-individually` check and enabling the `rust-coverage` functionality.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"now how is rust iteslf built\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thoughtSignature\":\"\",\"functionCall\":{\"name\":\"read_file\",\"args\":{\"absolute_path\":\"/data/data/com.termux.nix/files/home/pick-up-nix2/vendor/nix/flake.nix\"}}}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"parts\":[{\"functionResponse\":{\"id\":\"read_file-1761344582619-89fd4a1788046\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"response\":{\"error\":\"File path must be within one of the workspace directories: /data/data/com.termux.nix/files/home/pick-up-nix2/vendor/nix/union or within the project temp directory: /data/data/com.termux.nix/files/home/.gemini/tmp/98b630abdcd378fc27c9fe7a592684cc9353848d2a1c5ce29297dc12