    "response_text": "[{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thought\":true,\"text\":\"**Revising a Definition**\\n\\nI realized my mistake in `buildWorkspaceMember.nix`. I was trying to use functions from `cargo-toml-parsing.nix` in the `crateRepoSource` definition without passing them through. This won't work. I need to figure out how to properly pass `lib'.getIncludes` and `lib'.getExtraIncludes` to this scope.\\n\\n\\n\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thought\":true,\"text\":\"**Clarifying Argument Passing**\\n\\nI'm now rewriting `buildWorkspaceMember.nix`, incorporating `getIncludes` and `getExtraIncludes` as arguments. I'm focusing on ensuring `lib'` from `utils.nix` is used correctly, and that the arguments from `cargo-toml-parsing.nix` are correctly passed. I've corrected the `buildWorkspaceMember.nix` code to include these arguments.\\n\\n\\n\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thought\":true,\"text\":\"**Confirming Argument Implementation**\\n\\nI've successfully updated `buildWorkspaceMember.nix`. I've added `getIncludes` and `getExtraIncludes` as arguments, ensuring correct scope and argument passing. Now I'm checking that the build actually works as expected with the new implementation.\\n\\n\\n\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thought\":true,\"text\":\"**Addressing Function Availability**\\n\\nI've realized the problem lies in the availability of the functions within the `crateRepoSource` scope. I've now rewritten `buildWorkspaceMember.nix` to correctly pass `getIncludes` and `getExtraIncludes` as arguments. This addresses the function call error, ensurin