\n\\n\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thought\":true,\"text\":\"**Adjusting Function Access**\\n\\nI'm correcting the `buildWorkspaceMember.nix` file again, passing `getIncludes` and `getExtraIncludes` as arguments. I'm verifying the `lib'` usage and checking that the new implementation avoids the original error. The plan is to ensure everything is connected correctly for the `crateRepoSource` scope.\\n\\n\\n\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thought\":true,\"text\":\"**Addressing Code Corrections**\\n\\nI've rewritten the `buildWorkspaceMember.nix` file, specifically including the `getIncludes` and `getExtraIncludes` arguments. I'm making sure these functions are now passed and correctly utilized within the `crateRepoSource` definition. The main goal is to avoid the original errors.\\n\\n\\n\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thought\":true,\"text\":\"**Adjusting Argument Integration**\\n\\nI'm correcting the `buildWorkspaceMember.nix` file again, passing `getIncludes` and `getExtraIncludes` as arguments. I'm also confirming that the `lib'` from `utils.nix` is correctly used within the `crateRepoSource` scope. I'm focusing on ensuring everything is now connected correctly.\\n\\n\\n\"}]},\"citationMetadata\":{\"citations\":[{\"startIndex\":9620,\"endIndex\":9949,\"uri\":\"https://github.daw.org.cn/unionlabs/union/blob/main/tools/rust/crane.nix\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thought\":true,\"text\":\"**Revising Argument Correction**\\n\\nI've rewritten `buildWorkspaceMember.nix` again. This time, I'm passing `getIncludes` and `getExtraIncludes` as arguments, ensuring correct scope within `crateRepoSource`. I am also verifying that the `lib'` from `utils.nix` is correctly used. Now I am working to ensure everything is set up to build correctly.\\n\\n\\n\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thought\":true,\"text\":\"**Addressing Incorrect Imports**\\n\\nI've rewritten the `buildWorkspaceMember.nix` file, passing `getIncludes` and `getExtraIncludes` from `cargo-toml-parsing.nix` as arguments, which solves the initial error. I'm now testing the updated code to ensure that everything is working as expected within the `crateRepoSource` scope.\\n\\n\\n\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thought\":true,\"text\":\"**Adjusting Code Scope**\\n\\nI'm correcting the `buildWorkspaceMember.nix` file again, passing `getIncludes` and `getExtraIncludes` as arguments. I'm focusing on properly integrating the functions from `cargo-toml-parsing.nix` and ensuring the arguments are correctly used within the `crateRepoSource` definition.\\n\\n\\n\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thoughtSignature\":\"\",\"functionCall\":{\"name\":\"write_file\",\"args\":{\"file_path\":\"/data/data/com.termux.nix/files/home/pick-up-nix2/vendor/nix/union/tools/rust/crane-lib/buildWorkspaceMember.nix\",\"content\":\"\\n{ pkgs, lib', rust, inputs, craneLib, dbg, gitRev,\\n  isListOf, crateCargoToml, workspaceCargoToml, getMemberDeps, getAllDeps,\\n  cleanCargoLock, writeTOML, readMemberCargoTomls, mkCleanSrc,\\n  getIncludes, getExtraIncludes, # <--- Added these\\n  ... }:\\n\\nlet\\n  # sig :: string -> attrs -> drv\\n  buildWorkspaceMember =\\n    # the directory that contains the Cargo.toml and src/ for the crate,\\n    # relative to the repository root, or a list of multiple crates.\\n    crateDirFromRoot:\\n    {\\n      # a suffix to add to the package name.\\n      pnameSuffix ? \\\"\\\",\\n\\n      # the pname to use for this derivation if building multiple packages.\\n      pname ? null,\\n      # the version to use for this derivation if building multiple packages.\\n      version ? null,\\n\\n      # extra args to be passed to cargo build.\\n      cargoBuildExtraArgs ? \\\"\\\",\\n\\n      # if set to a string, the crate will be built for the specified target and will\\n      # rebuild the std library. incompatible with `cargoBuildRustToolchain`.\\n      buildStdTarget ? null,\\n      # update the toolchain that will be used for cargo build. defaults to\\n      # rust.toolchains.nightly if not set. incompatible with `buildStdTarget`.\\n      cargoBuildRustToolchain ? null,\\n\\n      # rustflags to be passed to cargo build.\\n      rustflags ? \\\"\\\",\\n\\n      # checkPhase to be passed to the cargo build derivation.\\n      cargoBuildCheckPhase ? null,\\n      # installPhase to be passed to the cargo build derivation.\\n      cargoBuildInstallPhase ? null,\\n\\n      # standard postBuild phase.\\n      postBuild ? null,\\n      # standard postInstall phase.\\n      postInstall ? null,\\n\\n      # extra environment variables to pass to the derivation.\\n      extraEnv ? { },\\n      # extra environment variables to pass to the derivation, only for crane.buildPackage.\\n      extraBuildEnv ? { },\\n\\n      extraBuildInputs ? [ ],\\n      extraNativeBuildInputs ? [ ],\\n\\n      # this builder will by default remove dev-dependencies from the Cargo.toml of all crates in the filtered source of the packages being built. set this to true to disable this behaviour.\\n      dontRemoveDevDeps ? false,\\n\\n      # the root Cargo.toml may require patching when b