    "response_text": "[{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thought\":true,\"text\":\"**Confirming the Intent**\\n\\nI've got the intent clear now: reuse the `openssl` and `pkg-config` parts in a new project and add a `README` for clarity. Confirmed that I'm working with new files and updating the old `crane.nix`.\\n\\n\\n\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thought\":true,\"text\":\"**Defining the Scope**\\n\\nNow I am narrowing the focus. I will be working on `common-rust-deps.nix` and constructing a `README.md` to explain its function and usage, which should directly address the user's needs. I should also check with the user if they still need me to break down `crane.nix` or if the new `common-rust-deps.nix` satisfies their needs for now. Refactoring `crane.nix` is complex and not a priority.\\n\\n\\n\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thought\":true,\"text\":\"**Prioritizing Documentation & Reuse**\\n\\nThe `README.md` is taking shape. I'm adding instructions on importing and integrating `common-rust-deps.nix` into a Nix flake. The example shows how to replace the original dependencies. Now, to make the guide comprehensive, I'm adding a section on environment variable setup.\\n\\n\\n\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thought\":true,\"text\":\"**Creating the Guide**\\n\\nI'm now writing the `README.md` in `tools/rust/README.md`. It explains `common-rust-deps.nix`, how to import it, and how to use it within a Nix flake, including examples for replacing existing dependencies and setting `PKG_CONFIG_PATH`. This should allow straightforward integration of the dependencies into a new project, which directly addresses the user's immediate need.\\n\\n\\n\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"thoughtSignature\":\"\",\"text\":\"Yes, that's correct. I've created the new file `tools/rust/common-rust-deps.nix` and was in the process of refactoring `crane.nix` to use it and to break it into smaller files.\\n\\nGiven your clarification that you primarily need to reuse the\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\" `openssl` and `pkg-config` part in another project, I will now create a `README.md` file in `tools/rust/` to explain the purpose and usage of `common-rust-deps.nix`.\\n\\nAfter that, I'd like to confirm if you still want me to proceed with the\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\" extensive refactoring of `crane.nix` into many smaller files, or if the `common-rust-deps.nix` and its documentation are sufficient for your current needs.\\n\\nFirst, let's create the `README.md`:\\n\"}]}}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\"},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"},{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"functionCall\":{\"name\":\"write_file\",\"args\":{\"content\":\"# Reusable Rust Dependencies for Nix\\n\\nThis directory contains Nix files designed to provide reusable definitions for common Rust-related dependencies and configurations.\\n\\n## `common-rust-deps.nix`\\n\\nThis file exports an attribute set containing common build inputs and environment variables related to `openssl` and `pkg-config`, which are frequently required for Rust projects.\\n\\n### Usage:\\n\\nTo use `common-rust-deps.nix` in your Nix flake or derivation:\\n\\n1.  **Import the file:**\\n    ```nix\\n    # In your flake.nix or a module\\n    let\\n      # Assuming 'pkgs' and 'lib' are in scope from your Nixpkgs import\\n      commonRustDeps = import ./tools/rust/common-rust-deps.nix { inherit pkgs lib; };\\n      inherit (commonRustDeps) commonBuildInputs pkgConfigPath;\\n    in\\n    # ...\\n    ```\\n\\n2.  **Integrate into `buildInputs`:**\\n    Replace explicit `pkgs.pkg-config`, `pkgs.openssl`, and the conditional Darwin security framework with `commonBuildInputs`.\\n\\n    **Example:**\\n    ```nix\\n    buildInputs = commonBuildInputs ++ [\\n      # other build inputs specific to your project\\n      pkgs.some-other-dependency\\n    ];\\n    ```\\n\\n3.  **Set `PKG_CONFIG_PATH`:**\\n    Use `pkgConfigPath` for setting the `PKG_CONFIG_PATH` environment variable.\\n\\n    **Example:**\\n    ```nix\\n    PKG_CONFIG_PATH = pkgConfigPath;\\n    ```\\n\\nThis approach centralizes the management of these common dependencies, making your Nix expressions cleaner and more maintainable across different Rust projects.\\n\",\"file_path\":\"/data/data/com.termux.nix/files/home/pick-up-nix2/vendor/nix/union/tools/rust/README.md\"}}}]},\"finishReason\":\"STOP\"}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"promptTokenCount\":69806,\"candidatesTokenCount\":588,\"totalTokenCount\":71218,\"cachedContentTokenCount\":68647,\"trafficType\":\"ON_DEMAND\",\"promptTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":69806}],\"cacheTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":68647}],\"candidatesTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":588}],\"thoughtsTokenCount\":824},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-flash\"}]",
